	{
		version = "0.5.45",
		lines = {
			"\001What's new\002 now lists every change of the newest three versions with notes, newest first; only the older versions are still cut after 40 lines with their 'And N more' line. After this update the window shows all 121 changes of 0.5.44 instead of 40.",
			"\001What's new\002 has two small buttons at the top right, as '< 0.5.43' and '0.5.45 >', that step to the version before and after in place, skip versions with no notes and keep the window where it was dragged. \001What's new in 0.5.45\002 on \001Home\002 and /flatui new open the newest version that has notes, so a build-only hotfix no longer opens on 'No notes for this version here.'.",
			"In \001What's new\002, a line that names a setting lights under the mouse and the footer says 'Click: open Number of bars in the options.'. A click closes What's new and opens the options window on that tab, scrolled to the row and flashing, as a search result does. Lines that name no setting stay plain.",
			"\001What's new\002 has a \001Filter\002 box above the list that keeps only the changes that mention every word typed ('party', 'threat list'). The line under the title says '12 of 121 changes mention \"party\".', versions with no match fold away, and clearing the box brings everything back.",
			"\001#changed\002 in \001Search\002 (and Home's \001Every change\002) now follows each reset arrow, Ctrl+Z and Ctrl+Y at once: the head counts down ('36 changed settings', then 'Every setting is at its default now'). A row back at its default dims to half and lights again if Ctrl+Z changes it back, and the list is made afresh at the next search.",
			"\001#changed\002 with more words narrows the list to the changed settings they match: '#changed nameplate' (or /flatui #changed nameplate) lists them under '9 changed settings for \"nameplate\"' with those words lit, and says 'No changed setting matches.' when none does. Before, any second word found nothing.",
			"\001Home\002's module tiles now count changed settings the same way as the tab dots and \001#changed\002. A tile no longer says 'Defaults' while \001Top trinket slot\002 is ticked, and no longer counts rows that #changed leaves out.",
			"\001Switch automatically\002 now says why it switched: 'Flat UI: switched to Raid, the profile for dungeons (Profiles > Switch automatically).', also in the options strip while the window is open. The first login of a session now applies the rules for where the character stands, so a character who logged out in a raid and logs in outside it goes to the profile of \001Everywhere else\002; a /reload keeps the profile in use.",
			"The test mode bar's title counts what it draws, as 'Test mode · 14 samples', and follows as samples come and go. Pointing at it names them ('Shows now: Party frames, Focus frame, Threat list... and 6 more.'). After a double-click on the title its tooltip adds 'Back at its place.'. The \001End\002 tip now says that your settings stay as they were and the bar keeps its \001Group\002 and place.",
			"A search typed in a fight before the options window was first opened, as '/flatui border colour', is no longer lost: chat says 'Flat UI: the options window opens after the fight, with your search.' and the window opens as the fight ends with the search run and lit. /flatui options in a fight now opens the game's options after it, and every such line reads the same way ('Flat UI: the welcome screen opens after the fight.', 'Flat UI: setup opens after the fight.').",
			"New \001Energy tick\002 (off), on the \001Player frame\002 tab. For a rogue, or a druid in Cat Form, a thin spark crosses the energy bar every 2 seconds and reaches its right end as the next energy comes in, where a second spark flares the way the \001Five-second rule\002 spark does, so they can time an opener, a Sinister Strike or a finishing move. It finds the beat from the first rise of 15 energy or more, keeps it in a fight and at full energy, and pays no heed to energy from Relentless Strikes or Thistle Tea. It hides in other forms, for other classes and before the first tick. A druid in Cat Form with both rows on sees the five-second rule on the druid mana bar and the tick on the energy bar. Turning it on in a fight waits for the end, and while the options window is open chat says so once. Test mode loops it, and setup's \001Player and target frames\002 step draws it 60% of the way across a rogue's or Cat Form druid's energy bar.",
			"\001Health text\002 and \001Power text\002 at \001Missing\002 now follow \001Number style\002: a party member down 4,523 health reads \"-4.5K\", or \"-4,523\" with 12,345, where before it read \"4523\". The text is blank at full, also in a fight, and setup's samples match.",
			"\001Show\002 at \001While not full\002 now hides a warrior's or bear's rage text while the rage is empty and shows it once rage builds, where before a \"0\" stayed all the time; mana and energy still hide at full. Setup's warrior sample matches. The \001Show\002 tip now says it works with a \001Health text\002 or \001Power text\002 format chosen on a frame's page, not with As the game has it.",
			"An enemy someone else has tapped, which gives no experience or loot, now turns grey as the game's own frames grey it: in the name row of the target, focus, target of target and boss frames, in a \001Health bar colour\002 of Reaction or Class and under \001Health in class and reaction colour\002, and in a \001Name colour\002 of Reaction or Class. It takes the \001Tapped by another player\002 colour of the \001Colours\002 page, also while \001Custom reaction colours\002 is off. Before, the mob showed hostile red. It turns back if the tap drops.",
			"In a fight with the options window open, \"Flat UI: the pet frame takes its new size when the fight ends.\" now shows only when \001Custom pet frame size\002 or its \001Percent\002 really changes the pet frame's size, no longer for every unit frame or Flat UI row changed, and no longer for a class with no pet.",
			"New \001Border for your focus\002 (off), with \001Focus border colour\002 (orange, the nameplates' focus colour), under \001Party and raid frames\002 on the \001All frames: icons and auras\002 tab. It outlines the party frame or raid cell of the member you have as your focus, also in a fight, and moves as the focus changes. When the focus is also your target, the border for your target stays on top. Setup's \001Boss and raid frames\002 step draws Bex as the focus while the row is on.",
			"More \001Unit frames\002 rows now show a tip: all four rows of the \001Raid frames\002 tab (\001Out of range opacity\002, \001Role icon\002, \001Name\002, \001Status text\002), \001Incoming heals\002, \001Absorb shields\002, \001Heal absorbs\002, the \001Looks\002 rows from \001Health in class and reaction colour\002 to \001Shadow behind each frame\002, \001Aura icon crop\002, \001Border colour by debuff type\002, \001Countdown numbers on party and pet debuffs\002, \001Leader icon\002, \001Role icon on player and party frames\002, \001PvP icon\002, \001Dead text\002, \001Totem time left\002, \001Totem cooldown swipe\002, \001Resting animation\002, \001Combat icon\002, \001Happiness face\002, \0013D head framing\002, \001Level colour\002 and \001Level size\002, as well as \001Name row colour\002 and \001Name colour\002, each saying in one sentence what it changes and on which frames.",
			"\001Pet target frame\002: \001Highlight under the mouse\002 now eases in over 0.08 seconds and out over 0.15 there too, as on the other frames, instead of snapping on and off. With \001Colour health bars by health left\002 on, its bar runs green through yellow to red as the enemy loses health, where before it stayed reaction red, and the Training Dummy of test mode and setup takes the 65% colour.",
			"The unit frames' hooks on the game's unit frame and raid cell functions, on the aura border and on the totem timer now go through Flat UI's shared hook helpers, so they skip while taint logging is on like every other hook. What the frames show does not change.",
			"Nameplates: New \001Flash as you take an enemy back\002 (on), under \001Mark enemies you are losing\002 on the \001Threat\002 tab. While you tank, as an enemy someone else held turns back to you, its glow flashes once in \001Threat you want\002, without the arrow, and fades over about half a second, so you see your taunt land. Before, the glow and arrow just faded away, the same as when the enemy left.",
			"Nameplates: the arrow of \001Mark enemies you are losing\002 now stands over an \001Above\002 quest mark instead of sitting on its !. It moves up or down as soon as the Overpower icon, an \001Above\002 threat value or the quest mark shows or goes. Before, it stayed under the icon, or hung over a gap until the enemy's threat changed.",
			"Nameplates: the number on the Overpower, Mongoose Bite or Riposte icon (\001Seconds on the Overpower icon\002) turns amber at 2 and red at its last second, and is a little dimmer while the icon is grey. When the game ends a Riposte or Mongoose Bite window early, the number now fades out with the icon instead of vanishing at once. Test mode's sample counts in the same colours; Setup's still sample keeps its white 3.",
			"Nameplates: New \001Line at Low health below\002 (on), on the \001Colours\002 tab under \001Health left\002. A thin line in \001Low health border colour\002 crosses each enemy's health bar at \001Low health below\002 (20% by default), so a warrior sees Execute range coming before the border lights. It moves at once with the slider, and the \001Low health\002 sample of Setup's \001Nameplate colours and threat\002 step shows it.",
			"Nameplates: every row of the nameplate pages now has a tip that says what it changes, from \001Restyle nameplates\002 and \001Nameplate style\002 to \001Health text format\002 and the class icon rows. Each game row's tip ends with where the game keeps the setting: for your account; for each character, so an alt has its own (\001Nameplate distance\002, \001Target nameplate scale\002, \001Far nameplate scale\002, \001Far nameplate opacity\002, \001Opacity behind obstacles\002); or on this computer (\001Horizontal overlap\002, \001Vertical overlap\002, \001Opacity of other nameplates with a target\002).",
			"Nameplates: with \001Show name\002 off, the Overpower icon, the arrow of \001Mark enemies you are losing\002, an \001Above\002 quest mark and an \001Above\002 threat value now sit just over the health bar, or over the debuffs while they show. Before, they hung a name's height higher over an empty band. They move back up when \001Show name\002 turns on.",
			"Nameplates: game rows whose setting the game locks or keeps read-only are no longer offered, in the options or in Setup. On WoW: Forever that is \001Cast bars on nameplates\002, which only printed \"Flat UI: the game kept Cast bars on nameplates on.\" after each click.",
			"Nameplates: /flatui status has a line for \001Mark enemies you are losing\002 and \001Enlarge enemies you are losing\002. It counts the enemies marked lost and slipping, the plates enlarged, the glows that grew while the game kept their plate, and the plates that waited for the end of a fight. While you do not count as a tank it says the marks are off.",
			"Nameplates: /flatui role now answers \"Flat UI: nameplate threat reads you as a tank (Defensive Stance).\" in place of \"Nameplate threat: you count as ...\". While you tank with \001Mark enemies you are losing\002 on, it adds \", so enemies you are losing are marked\". Its line for threat being off now starts with \"Flat UI:\" too.",
			"\001Sound when your interrupt lands\002 now plays when the game names you or your pet as the one who stopped the cast, on any enemy, nameplates too, and for a stun or silence of yours. A kick that came late or after another player's kick stays silent, where before it could still play. When the game keeps the name secret, it still follows the target or focus bar turning Interrupted, now only right after your interrupt.",
			"New \001Your interrupts\002 (on/off, off by default, on the \001Scroll areas\002 tab of \001Combat text\002): \"Interrupted\" with the icon of your Kick, Counterspell, Pummel or your pet's Spell Lock pops into the Outgoing area in \001Interrupt ready colour\002 each time your interrupt stops a cast. /flatui status counts them (\"Your interrupts in the Outgoing area: 4 shown.\").",
			"\001Sound when your focus casts\002 and \001Sound when your target casts\002 now also play, once a cast, as your interrupt comes back or you come into range while the cast runs, so a Kick back with 2 seconds of a Shadow Bolt Volley left is heard. Without \001Flat fill\002, the interrupt strip blinks once as it turns to \001Interrupt ready colour\002 then. /flatui status says how many played this way.",
			"\001Spell name alignment\002 now works on your own cast bar while \001Custom player cast bar size\002 is on (the default): \001Left\002 and \001Right\002 put the spell name at the bar's ends, inside or below it, clear of \001Cast time on your bars\002. \001As the game has it\002 and \001Centre\002 look the same as before. Setup's cast bar picture follows it.",
			"Personal resource display: the shield on the health bar now glides down over about a quarter second as hits eat it, as the \001Absorb shields\002 bars do. A new shield, the test sample and the first draw still fill at once.",
			"Personal resource display: \001Shield amount\002 now sits beside the health number, inside the bar (\"+1,234 12,345\"), where before it ran off the bar's right end. With only the percent showing, it still follows the percent.",
			"\001Seconds until your interrupt is ready\002 now also counts down your Felhunter's Spell Lock for a warlock. If the game gives no cooldown for the pet's spell, nothing shows, as before.",
			"Swing timers: with \001Show the timer\002 at \001In combat\002 (the default), the timers now fade out over a quarter second as the fight ends, where before they vanished at once. With \001Border around\002 at \001Whole timer\002, the border now fades with the bar, also with \001Only while swinging\002. When Edit Mode's own Visibility is In combat, the game still hides the timer at once.",
			"Test mode: the target's sample cast bar now fills as a ready cast, turns Interrupted as if kicked, then shows an uninterruptible cast. The first round of a session plays \001Sound when your target casts\002 as the cast starts and \001Sound when your interrupt lands\002 as it is kicked, once each.",
			"New \001Bars come back together\002 (off), under \001Fade\002 on the \001Fading\002 page. With it on, pointing at any faded action bar, the stance bar, the pet bar or Flat UI's page arrows brings every faded bar back to full in a tenth of a second. Once the mouse leaves, they wait \001Wait before fading\002 and fade down together. Before, only the bar under the mouse came back, so a key on bar 2 had to be found at 30% or 0%. Bars in a block that fades still follow the \001Bar block\002 page.",
			"\001Bar block\002: new \001Full opacity until health and mana are full\002 (off, needs \001Fade the block\002). It keeps the block, its panel and Flat UI's experience bar under it at full while your health, or your mana if you have a mana pool, is under full, so the bars are there while you eat and drink. Once both are full the block waits \001Wait before fading\002 and fades. Before, the \001Fading\002 page's \001Until health and mana are full\002 did not reach the bars of a block that fades. It does not hold while you are dead.",
			"Cooldown icons: \001Move a spell left\002 and \001Move a spell right\002 now move a spell past the next icon that really shows on its own row. Spells on another row and spells the character does not know yet keep their places. The strip says \"Recklessness is now number 1 of row 1.\" (\"of the row\" while rows 2 to 4 are off) or \"Recklessness is first on its row already.\". Before, a press could swap it with a spell on another row or one not shown, the row looked the same, and the number counted hidden spells. A spell not known yet says it has no place on the row.",
			"Cooldown icons: the lists of \001Move a spell left\002 and \001Move a spell right\002 show each spell's place on its row, as \"2. Recklessness\" or \"1. Death Wish (row 2)\", and \"(not known)\" with no number for a spell not learned yet.",
			"Cooldown icons: the look preview and test mode now show the sample buff time and proc glow on every row. The second icon of each row loops the sample buff time (8 of 12 seconds left) in \001Buff time colour\002, and the third glows in the \001Glow style\002 of the \001Proc alerts\002 page. This happens also when those icons are your own spells, trinkets or items, and they go back to the real buff time and proc when the preview ends. Before, only the sample icons of an empty row showed them, so on a row full of spells a change of \001Buff time on icons\002, \001Buff time colour\002 or \001Glow on procs\002 still seemed to do nothing.",
			"\001Proc alerts\002: the number of \001Seconds left on the button\002 now takes the \001Hotkey size\002 and \001Button text outline\002 of the \001Button text\002 page. It sits in the first corner the hotkey, macro name and count leave free: top left while the hotkey is at the top right (the default), top right while it is top left, and a bottom corner while the hotkey or macro name is at the top. Before, it was a fixed small number at the top centre, where a long key such as s-WU, or a hotkey or macro name at the top, ran into it. For its last 2 seconds it turns white and grows a little, so the proc is seen running out.",
			"\001Proc alerts\002: using a proc with seconds left no longer makes the number blink off at once. It keeps its last value and fades out with the glow.",
			"\001Proc alerts\002: with \001Glow style\002 set to \001As the game has it\002, the glow and its burst take the button's size each time they play. They fit Flat UI's buttons again after \001Button size\002 on the \001Bar block\002 page or Edit Mode's icon size changes, with no reload. Before, they kept the size of the button when it first glowed.",
			"\001Proc alerts\002: in test mode, a proc that is really up while test mode holds the same sample proc now counts its real seconds on the button and holds its faded bar or block at full, as outside test mode. Only the sample on its own loops its count and is left out of the fade.",
			"\001Action bars\002: a change of \001Button background\002, \001Icon crop\002, \001Button border\002, \001Empty buttons\002, \001Faint empty button opacity\002, \001Mouse over colour\002, \001Pressed colour\002 or \001Active colour\002 made in a fight with the options window open now says once: \"Flat UI: action buttons take their new look when the fight ends.\". Before, nothing seemed to happen until the fight ended.",
			"Tips for the rows of the \001Action bars\002, \001Button text\002, \001Colours and cooldowns\002, \001Bar block\002 and \001Cooldowns\002 pages that had none. Examples are \001Active colour\002 (auto attack, Auto Shot, a stance or form, or the spell being cast), \001Own usability colours\002, \001Not enough power colour\002, \001Button text outline\002, \001Stack direction\002, \001Line up bars\002, \001Faded opacity\002 and \001Icons per row\002.",
			"Fix: \001Show at a ready check or pull countdown\002 now catches a player's pull countdown, from /countdown or the raid frame manager's pull. Low and missing trackers come up as the count starts, a moment later one line names them ('Flat UI: before Ivo's pull, Mana Gem is low.'), and a cancelled countdown hides them again. Before, the game's countdown never reached the trackers.",
			"\001Show at a ready check or pull countdown\002: at a ready check the trackers stay up while the check is open, until it finishes or times out, instead of a fixed 12 seconds. They still stay up at least 12 seconds, so an all-ready leaves time to fix things, and the pull still ends them at once.",
			"Fix: the durability tracker's ready check reminder (low at 40%, shown whatever \001Show\002 says) now opens with the trackers' own reminder, at a ready check or a pull countdown, and ends at the pull with the rest. It no longer stays up into the fight for a few seconds, even with \001Hide in combat\002 on, and the 'before the pull' line names durability too.",
			"The ready check and pull countdown line names who lacks a group buff when 3 or fewer do, in class colours: 'Flat UI: for the ready check, Arcane Brilliance is missing on 2 of 5 (Eli, Mara).'",
			"\001Click to apply\002 conjures a missing or low Mana Gem, water, food, Healthstone or Soulstone out of combat, with the best spell the player knows for it. The tooltip reads 'A click casts Conjure Mana Ruby.', or that they lack its reagent while they have no Soul Shard. An item no spell makes, such as an Ankh, takes no click and no longer promises one in its tooltip.",
			"\001Click to apply\002 turns minimap tracking back on: a click on the red \001Tracking\002 tracker casts the tracking they last had on, such as Find Herbs or Track Beasts, and says when they cannot cast it now. Its choices now read \001Buffs, forms, pet, conjuring and tracking\002 and \001Buffs, forms, pet, conjuring, tracking and weapons\002.",
			"A pull ends /flatui tracker test at once, giving the trackers back their live state with one line, 'Trackers: the pull ended the test.' A /flatui test icons cut by the pull now says 'Defensives on you: the pull ended the test.' instead of the sweep and sound line.",
			"Fix: \001Your buffs\002, \001Sound when one ends\002 now plays for their own defensives too, such as Ice Barrier, Shield Wall, Evasion or Barkskin, also while \001Defensives on you\002 shows their icons. Before, these were silent at default settings. A buff that lasts longer than \001Time limit\002 is left out, as it is from the row.",
			"\001Your buffs\002: in /flatui test icons the first sample plays \001Sound when one ends\002 as its sweep runs out at 4 seconds, and the chat line names it ('Your buffs: three sample icons for 8 seconds. The first one ending plays Alarm.').",
			"\001Group tools\002: the pull button now counts down for every player countdown in the group, whether it was started by the row's button, the key binding or another player's /countdown, and stops when someone cancels it. Before, only test mode's sample counted down. Its tooltip names who started it: \"Mara counts down: 7 seconds left. Right-click stops it.\"",
			"\001Threat list\002: as a tank with \001List\002 at \001Your target, then enemies you are losing\002, when you have no enemy as your target, your target's target or your tank's target, the list now shows your group on the enemy you are losing most (a Lost one first, else the closest Slipping one), with the other lost and slipping enemies under it. Before, the window faded out when your target died mid-pack and stayed gone until you pressed Tab. It also comes back within a second when an enemy turns Lost.",
			"\001Threat list\002: with \001Calm when another tank takes it\002, once another tank taunts an enemy from whoever pulled it off you, the red stops at once and the title goes back to the enemy's name. Before, your bar kept pulsing for the full 2 seconds and the title named the other tank in red.",
			"\001Threat list\002: while the list follows \001Follow your tank's target\002, the title names the tank after a dim dot, in a light shade of their class colour: \"Defias Pillager · Mara\".",
			"\001Threat list\002: when more than 4 enemies under your target are lost or slipping, a dim last line under the small rows counts the rest (\"+2 more, 1 lost, 1 slipping\"), in the lost colour while one of them is lost.",
			"\001Threat list\002: pointing at a group bar names the member in their class colour and says what their share means (\"86% of the threat that pulls aggro: at 100% they take it\", or \"Holds aggro\"), then the state that applies: your own bar and \001Warn at\002, who took the enemy from you, another tank who stays calm, who is close to your aggro, or that the game withholds the threat. The tooltip follows the values as they change, and clicks still go through to the world.",
			"\001Threat list\002: with \001Bars stack\002 at \001Up\002, the small rows of the enemies you are losing now sit above the title, inside the window, so the title and the group bars stay where they are as those enemies come and go. Before, the whole list jumped up and down. Nothing changes under \001Down\002.",
			"\001Healer mana\002: the title's average, \001Low mana at\002 and ready now count every healer, also those past \001Number of bars\002. A dim last line counts the healers not shown, with the lowest mana among them (\"+3 more, lowest 22%\"), red while that is under \001Low mana at\002. Test mode's Raid sample shows it at 5 bars.",
			"\001Enemy cooldowns\002: with \001Show\002 at \001Always, used ones dark\002, test mode's samples now show all three looks. The Kick is bright and ready, the Ice Block sweeps dark, and the Divine Shield is dim with the question mark of a use the game hides, its tooltip reading \"Ready or used: the game hides its use here.\"",
			"\001Ping bar\002: the button of a ping that goes out, by a click on the world, a Shift-click or its key, flashes white once, also with \001Cooldown swipe\002 off. A ping the game refuses for its wait does not flash.",
			"The tips of \001Warn when you lose aggro\002 and \001Place on nameplates\002 no longer say \"him\" or \"his\" for another player; they say \"them\" and \"their\".",
			"New \001Say when your bags fill\002 (on), on the Bags page under Window. The moment the last free slot of your backpack and normal bags fills, chat says once \"Flat UI: your bags are full (0 of 80 free).\", also with the bag window closed. Special bags such as quivers, soul bags and the keyring do not count. It says it again only after a slot frees up, and at most once in 10 seconds, so looting and selling never fill your chat.",
			"New \001Sound when your bags fill\002 (None by default; Bell, Chimes, Alarm or Raid warning), which plays with that line. Out of combat, picking one plays it.",
			"New \001Order in a section\002 (By kind), on the Bags page under Sections. It lines up the items of each section \001By kind\002 (as before), \001Best quality first\002, \001By name\002 or \001Highest item level first\002, in both windows and for all your characters, and the windows lay out again at once. Keep in place keeps the order of your bags, and Bag by bag is unchanged.",
			"Bags: tooltips under the bag and bank windows now change while you point at them. \001Sell junk\002 counts down as it sells (\"Selling: 5 items left.\", and the label reads \"Selling... 5\"), and its list shrinks with each sale. \001Deposit\002 and \001Take out\002 count down too, the gold and free slots tooltips show the new numbers, and the clean up button's tooltip drops its Sorting line when the sort ends.",
			"Bags: right-click the Junk title for \001Your sell list (5)\002 and \001Never sold (2)\002. Each opens a small menu of its items by name, also of items no longer in your bags, and a click takes one off with the same chat line as /flatui sell. Junk and the junk coins update at once.",
			"Bags: the width grip now stops at the widest the window can be on your screen, and starts from the width shown, so dragging back moves the window at once. At that limit its tooltip adds \"As many as fit on your screen.\"",
			"Bags: double-click the width grip to put the width back to 12 slots (16 for the bank). It is one change in \001Recent changes\002, so Ctrl+Z gives the dragged width back, and the grip's tooltip says \"Double-click: back to 12 slots.\" while the width is off its default.",
			"Bags: \001Sell junk\002's list and the Junk title's list now put the item that brings the most first, so a 40g grey sword no longer falls under \"and 3 more\". A price the game has not given yet shows as a dim \"?\". The Junk title lists its items with what each brings, open or folded, and while you point at \001Sell junk\002 the titles of sections with nothing to sell fade, as they do for a search.",
			"Bags: the empty title a put back leaves (\"Potions 0\") now shows only in the bag window, and goes as soon as Bring back finds nothing to bring back. Bring back in \001Items placed by hand\002 now flashes Back on the section in the bag window.",
			"Bags: \001Custom sections\002 now lists \"Stop keeping what \"#boe q>=uncommon\" finds in Auction\" under each section that keeps a search, with a line in chat. The title menu reads \"Keep what the search finds here, not \"#boe\"\" when it would replace a kept search. Bringing a section back from \001Deleted sections\002 flashes Back on it in the bag window.",
			"Bags: the gold under the bag window lights faintly under the mouse, like the currencies beside it. Its tooltip's This session line ends \"since 14:05\" (or 2:05 PM, as the game's clock is set), and the character you play is marked with a small square in your accent colour.",
			"Minimap: the name of who pings the map now reaches Flat UI and sits right by the ping, in their class colour, inside the round edge of a round map. Before, it could fail to show at all, or land mirrored across the map from the ping. Test mode's sample \"Bex\" now goes when test mode ends, and /flatui status says \"Ping names: the game gives addons no minimap pings here.\" where the game gives none.",
			"Minimap: while test mode is on, and in /flatui move with \001Samples\002 on, each ticked line by the minimap that has nothing real to show shows a sample at its place and \001Text size\002: \"45.2, 61.8\", a yellow \"Durability 42%\", \"62 fps 48 / 95 ms\" and \"14:05\". Coordinates in a dungeon and durability on repaired gear can now be placed. The addon buttons and the zone name make room for the samples, and pointing at one says \"A sample while test mode is on.\"",
			"Minimap: \001Coordinates on the world map\002 now sits on Flat UI's background inside its thin border (or the HUD's, with \001Own border and background\002) in place of a plain black box. Its text follows the \001Text size\002 of the \001Minimap\002 page, and the box grows with it.",
			"Fading: New \001While a key is held\002 (None by default, or Shift, Ctrl or Alt). Holding the key brings every faded frame back to full in a tenth of a second, including the target and focus frames, buffs and the tracker that a rule keeps faded, so a player can glance at a cooldown, the bag bar or the micro menu. Once they let go, the frames fade again after \001Wait before fading\002. It does nothing while they type in a box.",
			"Quests: New \001Quests ready in the count\002 (on). The quest count on the tracker now reads \"12/20 3 ready\", with \"3 ready\" in the experience bar's \001Quest colour\002. The count pulses once as another quest becomes ready to hand in in play, never at login, on a /reload or when the log loads late.",
			"Experience bar: changing \001Experience bar\002 between Flat UI's and the game's, or turning off \001Restyle the minimap and HUD\002, in a fight now says once a fight, while the options window shows, \"Flat UI: the experience bar changes when the fight ends.\" The change still lands as the fight ends.",
			"Experience bar: the quest stretch no longer lights up, and a faded bar no longer comes to full, when the quest log fills in late after a slow login or loading screen. The glow now shows only for quests that become ready while a player plays.",
			"Experience bar: while a hunter's pet is out and still below their level, the experience tooltip adds its experience, \"Pet, level 31: 4,210 / 9,800 (43%)\", kept up to date as the pet gains. A warlock's pet, or a pet at their level, adds nothing.",
			"Errors: with \001Hide error messages\002 on, an error line that repeats, such as \"Not enough mana\" or \"Out of range\", now flashes brighter for a fifth of a second on each repeat, as the game's own error text does, while the game's flash setting for repeated errors is on.",
			"/flatui move: while picking is on, \001Pick a frame\002 reads \001Stop picking\002 in the accent colour, and its tooltip says it stops picking without taking a frame. It turns back once a frame is taken with Alt, it is clicked again or the session closes.",
			"The web address box keeps the whole address selected after a click or an arrow key, so Ctrl+C always copies it before the box closes. In \001Copy recent chat\002, Ctrl+C after a plain click (or an arrow without Shift) now says \"Nothing is selected: drag over some lines, or press Ctrl+A for every line.\" in place of a false \"Copied what you selected.\"",
			"\001Duration format\002 on the \001Buffs and debuffs\002 page has a third choice, \001Minutes and seconds (28:41)\002: a buff or debuff under an hour shows minutes and seconds (28:41, 1:05), then plain seconds in its last minute; an hour or more keeps the short form (2h). \001Tenths below\002 and \001Red under\002 work as before, and test mode's sample buffs and debuffs match.",
			"New \001Carrot on a Stick while riding\002 (Off, \001Bottom trinket slot\002 or \001Top trinket slot\002) on the \001Trinket queue\002 page: getting on a mount puts Carrot on a Stick in that slot, and getting off puts their trinket back: the best ready one of the slot's list while its Auto queue is on, else the one it replaced (a trinket held by hand comes back as it was). Chat and \001Sound on a swap\002 name each swap (\"riding\", \"off the mount\"), the slot's square says \"Riding: Carrot on a Stick until you get off\", it waits for the end of a fight as every swap does, and a trinket changed by hand while riding stays until the next mount.",
			"\001Letters left while typing\002 no longer counts a link's colour code or an icon, so a line with links reads its true count, and the typed text now stops short of the number while it shows instead of running under it.",
			"An item tooltip no longer shows its count twice: the grey \"Count: 5 in bags, 25 with bank\" line of \001Item count in bags and bank\002 is left out while \001Counts in tooltips\002 on the \001Bags\002 page shows this character's own line with the bank.",
			"New \001Queue line on trinket tooltips\002 (on/off, on by default) on the \001Trinket queue\002 page: a trinket's tooltip, in the bags or on the Character window, ends with a dim line such as \"Trinket queue: 2nd of 4, top slot\", with \" · Stop\" or \" · kept 20 s\" from its entry and \" · Auto queue off\" while that slot's queue is off; a trinket in both lists gets a line for each.",
			"A double-click on the title bar of the \001Gear comparison\002 window puts it back at its first size and place (\"Gear comparison: the window is back at its first size and place.\"), and a double-click on the \001Trinket queue\002 window's title bar puts it back at its first place (\"Trinket queue: the window is back at its first place.\"). Pointing at either title bar names the double-click.",
			"Shift-click on the gear comparison's \001Overall\002 line now ends with \" vs [item]\" naming the item worn in the slot that line compares when \001Against\002 holds nothing, as the ring in Finger 1; there is no \"vs\" for an empty slot.",
			"\001Who cast a buff or debuff\002 names the owner of a group member's pet, as \"Cast by Mara's pet (Imp)\" with Mara in their class colour, and \"your pet\" in \"Cast by your pet (Wolf)\" is now in your class colour, like \"You\".",
			"The \001Hearthstone\002 slot of a data panel now takes a left click: out of a fight it uses your Hearthstone, as on an action bar. Its tooltip ends \"Click: use your Hearthstone.\" (\"Out of a fight, click: ...\" in one), the cooldown still counts down in the slot, a right click opens the slot menu as before, and with \001Tooltips\002 off the slot keeps its click.",
			"New \001Zone\002 choice for every data panel slot: the subzone, or the zone where there is none (\"Goldshire\"), green in a friendly zone, red in a hostile one, gold where it is contested and blue in a sanctuary. Its tooltip names the zone, the subzone, the state in words (\"Contested territory\") and your coordinates. A click opens the world map, and Shift-click puts \"Goldshire, Elwynn Forest 42.1, 65.9\" in chat.",
			"The \001Bag space\002 slot now opens or closes the game's bags on a click while the \001Bags\002 page is off, and its tooltip says what your junk fetches: \"To sell 6 items, 1g 4s\", with \"and 3 more of your sell list\" when more wait.",
			"New \001Clear a waypoint as you reach it\002 (on/off) on the Errands page: the pin /way set comes off as you arrive, a soft chime plays and chat says \"Flat UI: you reached the waypoint at Elwynn Forest 45.0, 61.0.\" It needs \001In-game navigation\002. A pin you put on the map yourself stays.",
			"\001Mount key\002: a press that has nothing to use, indoors, in a dungeon or on a character with no mount, now says why in chat, at most once every 10 seconds: \"Mount key: none of your mounts can be used here and now. ...\" or \"Mount key: no mount or travel form to use yet.\"",
			"\001Consumables bar\002: with \001Fade out of a fight\002, the bar now stays at full while the mouse moves between its buttons, with no flicker in the \001Spacing\002 gaps, and settles back once the mouse leaves the bar.",
			"\001Consumables bar\002: a key of the bar pressed while you hold an item on the cursor now uses nothing and leaves the item on the cursor. Before, letting the key go put the item on your list. Dropping an item with the mouse works as before.",
			"\001Glow size\002 changed in a fight now reaches the herb or vein that glows as the fight ends, and chat says once a fight, while the options window shows: \"Flat UI: the glow takes its new size when the fight ends.\"",
			"New \001Class colour\002 (on/off, off) under \001Cursor ring colour\002: paints the cursor ring in your class colour, so a rogue's pointer is yellow and a mage's light blue, and shows at once with the ring's preview.",
			"\001Lava tick timer\002: the dodge that beats your best streak of the session, from 3 on, now reads \"Best x7\" in gold with a brighter flash, in place of the green \"Dodged x7\".",
			"\001/flatui move\002: press on empty space and drag to select every box the rectangle touches, but for the boxes of frames the game places. It has a thin accent outline over a faint fill, and the boxes light up as you drag. Shift and drag adds them to the selection, Ctrl and drag takes them away, and a click on empty space lets go of them all. Shift or Ctrl and click on a box, or on a name in the frame list, adds it or takes it away; a plain click still selects one box alone.",
			"\001/flatui move\002: every selected box has the accent outline and every selected frame is marked in the frame list. Drag any of them and the others move with it by the same amount, keeping their places to one another and stopping together at the edge of the screen. With \001Snap\002 on, the box under the mouse snaps and the others follow it. The arrow keys move them all, Shift ten at a time.",
			"\001/flatui move\002: with two or more selected, the inspector reads \"3 frames selected\" and offers \001Align left\002, \001Align right\002, \001Align top\002, \001Align bottom\002, \001Centre horizontally\002 and \001Centre vertically\002 (on the middle of the space they cover together). It also has \001Distribute across\002 and \001Distribute down\002 (equal gaps in their order on the screen, with three or more) and \001Reset these\002.",
			"\001/flatui move\002: each group drag, align, distribute or \001Reset these\002 is one Undo step, and so is a run of arrow presses less than a second apart. Undo and Redo select the frames they put back. Hidden frames, frames not on screen now and frames placed by the game stay put in group moves and in \001Reset these\002; the inspector says how many, and chat says once which.",
			"\001/flatui move\002: Escape now lets go of the selection first and closes the boxes once nothing is selected. Ctrl and click no longer marks boxes for the lower \001Space across\002 and \001Space down\002 bar, which is gone: \001Distribute across\002 and \001Distribute down\002 in the inspector do the same for the selected frames.",
		},
	},
	{
		version = "0.5.44",
		lines = {
			"Nameplates: Enlarge enemies you are losing (on by default, under Mark enemies you are losing on the Threat tab). While you tank, the nameplate of an enemy on someone else grows to Size of an enemy you have lost (130% by default, from 100% to 160%), and one changing hands grows half as much. It eases over a fifth of a second about its own centre so it does not jump, rises above the plates around it, and shrinks back the same way as you take the enemy back.",
			"Nameplates: where the game keeps a plate from being changed in a fight, the plate keeps its size and the glow and arrow of Mark enemies you are losing grow by the same amount instead; the plate grows once the fight ends if the enemy is still lost.",
			"Nameplates: a plate the game hands to another enemy, a plate that hides, either row turned off, no longer counting as a tank and Flat UI's nameplates turned off all put the plate's size and layer back as they were.",
			"Nameplates: test mode's sample nameplate and the samples of Setup's Nameplate colours and threat step grow as live plates do on threat you do not want, and half as much on threat changing hands; Setup makes room for them and keeps each label beside its sample.",
			"Threat list: your group on your target is back for everyone, as before 0.5.43. \001List\002 has a new default, \001Your target, then enemies you are losing\002. It shows your group on your target with all its rows, colours, warnings and sounds. While you tank it also adds, under a thin line, up to 4 small rows for the other enemies you are losing: Lost ones first, then Slipping ones. Each row has the enemy's raid marker, its name, its colour and pulse, and who holds it or is closing in.",
			"Threat list: while one of those enemies is lost, the title adds a small \"· 1 lost\" after your target's name, as in \"Defias Pillager · 1 lost\". Nothing is added while no other enemy is lost or slipping, so a fight against one enemy looks as it always did.",
			"Threat list: the small rows count apart from \001Number of bars\002. A row flashes and plays \001Sound when you lose an enemy\002 when its enemy turns to Lost, and the rows move with \001Animate bars\002. Your target itself still has \001Warn when you lose aggro\002.",
			"Threat list: \001Enemies while you tank\002, the 0.5.43 default, is now \001Your target, then enemies you are losing\002, and profiles that had it move to the new choice. \001Enemies you fight\002 still shows only the enemies, and \001Your group on your target\002 shows your group on your target alone, without the enemies under it.",
			"Threat list: the enemies under your target are read at most five times a second, only in a fight and only while you tank. Test mode and /flatui threat show two sample enemies under the sample group, one lost and one slipping. In test mode the slipping one turns lost every 6 seconds.",
			"The tips of \001Calm when another tank takes it\002 and \001Show healer mana\002 now say \"they\" and \"their\" for the other player.",
			"\001Search\002 heads each group of results, and each page chip, with the page's place, as \"Flat UI > Colours\" and \"Nameplates > Colours\" in place of two groups both called \"Colours\", and a module's name now counts as a word of each of its tabs, so \"/flatui nameplate cast colour\" finds the colour rows of \001Nameplates > Cast bar\002; a tab's chip shows only when its module's chip does not already match.",
			"Typing \001#changed\002 in \001Search\002, or /flatui #changed, lists every setting of the profile in use that is off its default, grouped by page, each with its reset arrow; the head says how many (\"37 changed settings\"), or \"Every setting is at its default.\" A dim \001Every change\002 in Home's \001Recent changes\002 opens it, and pointing at the Search box says the word exists.",
			"With \001Replace the game's fonts\002 on and the options window open, changing a row that is not a Fonts row in a fight (\001Border colour\002, \001Bar texture\002...) no longer says \"Flat UI: fonts change when the fight ends.\"; the line shows only when a \001Fonts\002 row really changed.",
			"\001Export by module\002 has \001All\002 and \001None\002 above its module list, so None and one tick export a single module; the \001Modules\002 button reads \001Hide list\002 while the list is open, and \001Export chosen\002 with nothing ticked says \"Tick a module first.\"",
			"A right-click on any colour swatch offers \001Copy #D93A30\002 and, once a colour is copied, \001Paste #D93A30\002, which writes it at once, shows in \001Recent changes\002 and is undone with Ctrl+Z; the copied colour also leads the colour picker's recent colours.",
			"The test mode bar now opens with the \001Group\002 last picked on the account and at the place you dragged it to, also after a reload; a double-click on its title still puts it back and forgets the drag.",
			"A double-click on the options window's title bar puts the window back in the middle of the screen and forgets its saved place (\"The window is back in the middle.\").",
			"The test mode bar fades in and out instead of appearing and vanishing at once, and turning test mode on again while it fades out brings it straight back.",
			"/flatui profile answers now start with \"Flat UI:\", and a name it does not know lists the profiles: \"Flat UI: no profile named Raidd. Profiles: Default, Raid, Alt.\"",
			"\001Bar block\002: a block whose bars were moved or added now shows the changed dot and reset arrow on its \001Bars\002 row (\"Reset Bars: back to its default.\"), and the \"changed on this tab\" count goes to it, where before the count and the dots led to no row.",
			"\001Show\002, under \001Health and power text\002, has a third choice, \001While not full\002. The health text appears as soon as a unit takes damage and goes again once they are topped up, and the power text does the same for mana, also in a fight, so a party column stays clean until someone needs a heal. Dead, Ghost and Offline still always show. Setup's sample follows it.",
			"\001Colour health bars by health left\002 now also colours raid cells and raid-style party frames from green through yellow to red, also in a fight. Turned off, they take the game's colours back, and offline members keep the game's grey. Setup's \001Boss and raid frames\002 step draws the cells in those colours. The tip no longer says \"Not raid frames.\"",
			"The AFK count now stays with the member. Before, a raid cell that moved when someone joined or left started again at a bare \"AFK\", and on party frames the member who moved into party1 could take over the old member's \"AFK 12m\". Party and raid frames now agree. In a raid fight, frames no longer listen to every health change while nobody is away.",
			"\001AFK on raid frames\002: while the game's raid frame \001Display Health Text\002 shows health (Health, Health Lost or Percent), the AFK word now sits just above it in the middle of the cell instead of on top of it. With None it stays where the status text sits.",
			"Nameplate \001Low health border\002: a nameplate that first appears in a fight now queues one catch-up job, not one per health change, so the end of a long fight no longer hitches. With the options window open, chat no longer says \"the low health border shows when the fight ends.\" for nameplates, where no setting changed.",
			"\001Five-second rule\002: as the spark reaches the end of the mana bar it now flares, growing to about 1.6 times its size as it fades over 0.3 seconds, so you see regen come back. A spell cast before in the session still starts the sweep in a fight where the game withholds its cost. Test mode shows the flare in its one second rest.",
			"Changing \001Frame style\002, \001Portrait size\002, \001Space between parts\002, \001Name room\002, \001Level position\002, \001Corners\002 or \001Portrait shape\002 in a fight now says once, while the options window shows, \"Flat UI: unit frames take their new layout when the fight ends.\" \001Shadow behind each frame\002 says \"Flat UI: frame shadows show when the fight ends.\" and \001Custom pet frame size\002 says \"Flat UI: the pet frame takes its new size when the fight ends.\" A new target without a power bar or a pet summoned in a fight stays silent. The heal over time squares' \"show\" and \"move\" lines are now each said on their own, so one no longer hides the other in a fight.",
			"\001Highlight under the mouse\002 now eases in over 0.08 seconds and out over 0.15 as the mouse sweeps down the party or raid frames, instead of snapping on and off. With \001Show\002 at \001Under the mouse\002, the health and power text now fades in over 0.1 seconds and out over 0.15.",
			"Raid markers on party and raid frames now pop from about 1.6 times their size to their own over 0.2 seconds as one lands or changes, also in a fight, so a Skull or Moon placed on a member is noticed. Nothing pops at login, on zoning, on joining a group or for a new member in a cell.",
			"\001Squares for your heals over time\002: a square that lights as your heal lands, or is refreshed with a later end, now pops from about 1.5 times its size over 0.15 seconds, so a healer sees which frame took the heal. Squares read for the first time, at login, for a new member or as a fight ends, do not pop.",
			"New \001Enemy nameplates\002, \001Friendly player nameplates\002 and \001Friendly NPC nameplates\002 (off, as the game has them at first) and \001Always show nameplates\002 (on), at the top of \001Which show\002 on the \001Size and clicks\002 tab of \001Nameplates\002. These are the game's own switches, so plates that vanished after pressing V, or friendly plates for a battleground, can come back without leaving Flat UI. Each shows the game's live value, also after V or Shift+V. \001Nameplates on enemy pets and totems\002 and \001Nameplates on minor enemies\002 now grey out while Enemy nameplates is off, and \001Friendly players as names only\002 while Friendly player nameplates is off, as the game nests them.",
			"New \001Stack enemy nameplates\002 and \001Stack friendly nameplates\002 (off), under \001Size and stacking\002. They turn on the game's stacking, off on this client at first. The plates of a pulled pack now move apart up and down into a readable column instead of covering each other, and \001Horizontal overlap\002 and \001Vertical overlap\002 set their spacing while they stack. Setup's \001Nameplate size, distance and clicks\002 drawing shows the near plate over the target while Stack enemy nameplates is off and stacked above it while it is on.",
			"New \001Class colours on enemy players\002 and \001Class colours on friendly players\002 (off), under \001Reaction\002 on the \001Colours\002 tab of \001Nameplates\002. They turn on the game's class colours for players' health bars, a rogue yellow and a mage light blue, and nameplates repaint at once. The \001Players\002 tip now points to them. Setup's \001Enemy player\002 samples are hostile red while the enemy row is off. Before, they always took your own class colour. They take a class colour while it is on, the \001Friendly\002 samples follow the friendly row, and the colours drawing adds a \001Friendly player\002 sample while that row is on.",
			"New \001Aura size\002 (100%, 70% to 140%), on the \001Auras\002 tab of \001Nameplates\002. It sets the game's size of the buff and debuff icons on nameplates, so larger Rend, Sap or Rejuvenation icons need no trip to the game's options. The Overpower icon, an \001Above\002 threat value and an \001Above\002 quest mark rise with the taller row, and setup's \001Nameplate auras\002 drawing and preview band grow with it.",
			"New \001Seconds on the Overpower icon\002 (on), under \001Time left on the Overpower icon\002. A crisp white number in the middle of the Overpower, Mongoose Bite or Riposte icon counts its seconds left down over the swipe, 5 to 1, and starts again at 5 when a new dodge or parry renews it. Setup's \001Marks and icons\002 drawing shows a 3, and test mode's sample counts down.",
			"Riposte and Mongoose Bite now show grey from your parry or dodge while energy or mana is short, and their swipe counts from it. Before, a parry right after a Sinister Strike showed nothing until energy ticked in, up to 2 seconds later, and the swipe then claimed a full 5 seconds that the game had already cut short. The icon now lights up and glows as the energy or mana arrives.",
			"New \001Full points breathe\002 (on), under \001Full points colour\002 on the \001Marks and icons\002 tab. While you sit at your most combo points, the gold row breathes softly, from full to about half and back about once a second, and stops the moment a finisher spends them, so full points are not wasted in a busy fight. Setup's \001Full points\002 sample and test mode's sample breathe the same way.",
			"\001Health text format\002 at \001Missing\002 now leaves an unhurt enemy's nameplate blank, as the unit frames do. Before, every full-health enemy showed a 0. A hurt enemy still shows how much it is missing (\"1.2K\"), and setup's full sample matches.",
			"\001Show health text\002 at \001Only on the target\002 or \001On the target and focus\002 now eases the health number out on the old target and in on the new one over 0.15 seconds, with the aura rows, instead of blinking on Tab. A nameplate that appears, and a change of the options, still set it at once.",
			"Dragging a game setting of the nameplate pages in a fight now says so once a fight, while the options window shows: \"Flat UI: nameplate game settings change when the fight ends.\". This covers the rows under \001Which show\002, \001Size and stacking\002 and \001Scale and fade\002, \001Aura size\002 and the class colour rows. Before, the slider could jump back with no word, and the change still lands as the fight ends.",
			"And 81 more changes in the full changelog on CurseForge.",
		},
	},
	{
		version = "0.5.43",
		lines = {
			"Threat list: a new List row. At Enemies while you tank (the default), a tank sees a row for each enemy with a nameplate that you or your group fight, instead of the group. Each row has the enemy's raid marker, its name and a bar of your hold on it, and the ones you are losing come first.",
			"Threat list: in Enemies, an enemy someone else holds is Lost. It is red, pulses fast and names who holds it in their class colour with their share of your threat (\"Mage 112%\"). One where another member passes Slipping at (80% by default) turns amber and pulses slowly, naming who is closing in. Enemies you hold stay green, calm and a little dimmer.",
			"Threat list: Enemies outlines your target's row, and the title reads \"Threat: 3 enemies, 1 lost\". A last line counts the enemies past Number of bars, and an enemy that turns to Lost flashes and plays Sound when you lose an enemy (by default Warning sound, while Warn when you lose aggro is on, as in the group list). An enemy another tank holds stays calm.",
			"Threat list: Enemies reads five times a second in a fight and nothing out of one. Its rows take no clicks; pointing at one says who has the enemy and to click its nameplate. Enemies you fight shows it in every role, and Your group on your target keeps the list as it was.",
			"Threat list: Animate bars (on by default). Bars slide to each new value, rows glide to their new place and flash as they overtake another, the top bar has a faint sheen, and your group's names take a light shade of their class colour.",
			"Threat list: test mode and /flatui threat show four sample enemies in Enemies, one lost, one slipping and two held, and in test mode their states turn every 6 seconds.",
			"Nameplates: Mark enemies you are losing (on by default). While you tank, an enemy changing hands or on someone else pulses with a soft glow in its threat colour, faster once it is lost, under a small arrow pointing down at it. The sample nameplates of test mode and Setup show it too.",
			"New \001Absorb shields on the health bar\002 (Bright layer over the health), in a new \001Absorb shields\002 section of the \001Personal resource display\002 page. Your absorb shields now lie over the display's health bar as a silvery layer that starts where your health ends, with a thin bright edge where the shield ends. A shield bigger than your missing health runs on back over your health, so its full size still shows on the bar; at full health it runs in from the right end. \001Plain fill after the health\002 stops it at the end of the bar instead, and \001Off\002 takes it away.",
			"The shield layer has a slow \001Sheen\002 (on) that sweeps across it every few seconds. It flashes as a new shield lands or grows and fades quickly as it breaks, though not while the game withholds the amount, and \001Shield outline\002 (on) frames the whole health bar in \001Shield colour\002 while a shield is up. \001Shield colour\002 (a light silver blue) and \001Shield opacity\002 (60%) set its look, and \001Shield amount\002 (off) adds the amount after the health text, as +1,234, in the shield colour.",
			"The shield on the health bar works in a fight and uses the game's absorb total. On a client without one it shows the shields the \001Absorb shields\002 page tracks. Test mode lays a sample shield of about 35% of your health over the display, with its sheen, and setup's \001Personal resource display\002 step lists the new rows.",
			"New \001What's new\002 window: from now on, the first login after Flat UI updates shows what changed in each version since the one you last played on this account, newest first, with setting names in the accent colour. This first time it shows 0.5.43, as older versions kept no note of the one you played. It has \001Open Flat UI's options\002 and \001Close\002, Escape closes it, and it can be dragged anywhere on screen. It waits for the end of a fight, and if a fight starts it steps aside (\"Flat UI: What's new comes back after the fight.\") and comes back after it. A new install shows nothing, as the welcome screen and setup walk you through Flat UI.",
			"New \001What's new after an update\002, under \001Updates\002 on the \001Options and setup\002 tab of the \001Flat UI\002 page: \001Show the window\002 (the default), \001One line in chat\002 (\"Flat UI updated to 0.5.43. /flatui new shows what changed.\") or \001Nothing\002. A character the welcome screen greets gets the chat line instead of the window.",
			"New /flatui new (or /flatui changes) opens \001What's new\002 at any time with this version's changes, and /flatui new 0.5.41 shows that version, one of the newest six. \001What's new in 0.5.43\002, at the bottom of \001Home\002 in the options window, opens it too.",
		},
